CLASS:: FoaEncoderKernel
summary:: PHJ encoder extension for First Order Ambisonic (FOA) encoding
categories:: Libraries>Ambisonic Toolkit>Matrix & Kernel>FOA
related:: Classes/FoaEncoderKernel, Classes/FoaEncode

DESCRIPTION::
Extends FoaEncoderKernel with newPHJ method for kernel-based PHJ encoding.

PHJ (Periphonic UHJ) encoding uses 4-channel input (L,R,T,Q) and produces 
4-channel B-format output (W,X,Y,Z) with true height information.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: newPHJ
Ambisonic PHJ encoder using kernel-based processing.

argument:: kernelSize
256, 512, 1024, 2048, 4096, 8192

argument:: server
link::Classes/Server:: on which to load kernel.

argument:: sampleRate
The sample rate defaults to code::nil:: and is usually supplied by the running server.

argument:: score
Default is code::nil:: for most real time usages.

discussion:: 
PHJ encoding uses kernel-based processing with impulse response files located 
in ATK/kernels/FOA/encoders/phj/. This provides frequency-dependent encoding 
from 4-channel input (L,R,T,Q) to B-format (W,X,Y,Z).

note:: 
PHJ requires 4-channel input files for proper operation. The kernel files 
must be installed in the ATK kernels directory.::
